# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Web Design Stack — environment template
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then fill in only the keys you need.
#
# .env is git-ignored (.gitignore: `.env`, `.env.*`, with `!.env.example`).
# NEVER put a real key in this file. NEVER commit a key anywhere.
# Every server below degrades gracefully: leave a key blank and that provider
# is simply unavailable — the rest of the stack keeps working.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Image sourcing — `imagebank` MCP ─────────────────────────────────────────
# At least ONE of these is required for image search to return results.
# All three are free tiers. The server reports which providers are configured
# on startup ("Providers configured: ...").
#
# Pexels        https://www.pexels.com/api/          (free, no attribution required)
PEXELS_API_KEY=
# Unsplash      https://unsplash.com/developers      (free; ATTRIBUTION REQUIRED — see below)
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=
# Pixabay       https://pixabay.com/api/docs/        (free, no attribution required)
PIXABAY_API_KEY=
#
# Unsplash's API terms require attribution to the photographer and to Unsplash,
# with UTM-tagged links. The image-sourcing workflow records this in
# public/images/image-sources.json. Do not strip it.

# ── Image generation — `nanobanana` MCP (Google Gemini) ──────────────────────
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (free tier available).
# The server accepts either variable name; set GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY and leave the
# other blank unless a tool you use specifically wants GEMINI_API_KEY.
GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Component discovery — `21st` MCP ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate a key at https://21st.dev/mcp
# NOTE: keys issued by the old "Magic" console were reset upstream and no longer
# work. You need a current 21st key.
TWENTY_FIRST_API_KEY=

# ── Pinterest references — `pinterest` MCP ───────────────────────────────────
# The default config points at the maintainer's hosted Cloudflare Worker, which
# performs OAuth in your browser — no key goes in this file for that route.
#
# Only set these if you SELF-HOST the worker (see docs/INSTALL.md):
PINTEREST_CLIENT_ID=
PINTEREST_CLIENT_SECRET=
COOKIE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
